[agent] {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"configured-source","update":{"content":{"text":"","type":"text"},"_meta":{"agentComms":{"updates":[{"kind":"transcript_snapshot","page":{"events":[{"kind":"tool_end","routing":null,"source":null,"timestamp":1790716430.739,"tool_call_id":"call_t0AFh0YtcqSFGITO4lMe0n1t|fc_0c6f92b7d90e9065016abc2a0a057c87d2ad8cca6d33d34f22","tool_name":"edit","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in skills/refactor-audit/references/principles.md.","ok":true,"diff":{"text":"--- skills/refactor-audit/references/principles.md\n+++ skills/refactor-audit/references/principles.md\n@@ -50,5 +50,4 @@\n \n **14. Mechanize every recurring violation, and prove the measure first.** In one day across two agent-built repositories, agents respected the style wherever structure enforced it (debt density fell 19% and 38%, legacy code was deleted rather than renamed) and broke it wherever the rule was only written down (a revived compatibility adapter, an eleven-term validity chain, two codec forks, 75 new `None` checks). Each violation class stopped once it had a mechanical check. But measures need proving: to catch the `None` growth, a count of optional fields and then a count of optional attributes both fell while the checks rose. Only counting probes of *another object's* absent state tracked it (+81 against +75). Run a candidate measure at the heads where the violation grew before trusting it.\n \n **15. Enforce polymorphism by ratcheting its alternatives.** The plans for two agent-built repositories prescribed polymorphic targets surface by surface, each with guards for its own result, and enforced several antipatterns codebase-wide. They never ratcheted string dispatch or type switches, the direct alternatives to polymorphism. Across two days and 210 merges, agents mostly chose families anyway, but six merges added dispatch, and one feature merge added two string dispatches with nineteen string-keyed reads. Count candidate subjects per function (a subject compared against three or more literals; three or more type checks on one subject), and their distinct arms, so growth within an existing candidate is visible too. Prove both measures on known-bad changes and known-good refactors. Syntax does not establish ownership: inspect whether each taxonomy is external or a missing family. Counts are screening ratchets, not complete enforcement; subthreshold cases and additions offset by removals escape them. Once ownership is admitted, site-specific guards make the prohibited dispatch impossible to reintroduce.\n-\n","format":"unified"}},{"kind":"thinking","routing":null,"source":null,"timestamp":1790716455.663,"text":""},{"kind":"tool_start","routing":null,"source":null,"timestamp":1790716455.663,"tool_call_id":"call_MO2d279MttB3HlRFr5e6TSKE|fc_0c6f92b7d90e9065016abc2a1b45bc87d2861ab74dc874f393","tool_name":"bash","raw_input":{"command":"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom zipfile import ZipFile, ZipInfo, ZIP_DEFLATED\nroot = Path('skills/refactor-audit')\nfiles = sorted(p for p in root.rglob('*') if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ('.md', '.py') and '__pycache__' not in p.parts)\nwith ZipFile('skills/refactor-audit.skill', 'w') as archive:\n    for path in files:\n        info = ZipInfo(path.relative_to(root.parent).as_posix(), date_time=(1980, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0))\n        info.compress_type = ZIP_DEFLATED\n        info.create_system = 3\n        info.external_attr = 0o100644 << 16\n        archive.writestr(info, path.read_bytes())\nwith ZipFile('skills/refactor-audit.skill') as archive:\n    assert archive.testzip() is None\n    for path in files:\n        assert archive.read(path.relative_to(root.parent).as_posix()) == path.read_bytes()\nprint(f'Verified rebuilt archive against {len(files)} editable files')\nPY\ngit add -- skills/refactor-audit.skill skills/refactor-audit && git diff --cached --check && git diff --cached --stat\npython - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess\npaths = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'diff', '--cached', '--name-only'], text=True).splitlines()\nassert paths and all(p == 'skills/refactor-audit.skill' or p.startswith('skills/refactor-audit/') for p in paths), paths\nassert not any('__pycache__' in p for p in paths)\nprint('Staged paths limited to the skill package and editable source')\nPY","timeout":25}},{"kind":"tool_end","routing":null,"source":null,"timestamp":1790716457.538,"tool_call_id":"call_MO2d279MttB3HlRFr5e6TSKE|fc_0c6f92b7d90e9065016abc2a1b45bc87d2861ab74dc874f393","tool_name":"bash","text":"Verified rebuilt archive against 27 editable files\n skills/refactor-audit.skill                        | Bin 75316 -> 79174 bytes\n skills/refactor-audit/SKILL.md                     | 139 +++++\n .../refactor-audit/references/package-templates.md | 166 +++++\n .../refactor-audit/references/patterns/README.md   | 121 ++++\n .../references/patterns/agent-defaults.md          | 108 ++++\n .../references/patterns/boundaries.md              | 182 ++++++\n .../refactor-audit/references/patterns/identity.md | 203 ++++++\n .../references/patterns/implementation.md          | 553 +++++++++++++++++\n .../references/patterns/membership.md              | 166 +++++\n .../references/patterns/over-time.md               | 237 +++++++\n skills/refactor-audit/references/principles.md     |  53 ++\n skills/refactor-audit/references/rules-template.md |  80 +++\n .../refactor-audit/references/surface-receipt.md   | 111 ++++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/attribute_origin.py  |  53 ++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/__init__.py    |   1 +\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/census.py      |  73 +++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/chain_terms.py | 165 +++++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/family.py      |  55 ++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/findings.py    | 680 +++++++++++++++++++++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/measures.py    | 467 ++++++++++++++\n skills/refactor-audit/scripts/audit/origin.py      | 148 ++++